        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/tests/unit/test_doctor.py#L206-L216",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5ec11f0bd4832ad6e06787bb80a46282e0f4756defe3ede41b99b5025871ee2a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/doctor.py#L350-L362",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:94555914f3f115dcd74309042c3acde5b5e8af366da73572ecd5763c0da52ce8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8116f03b87654ac48da902a8b854738a",
      "statement": "A model id ending in `-latest` is refused at boot for either VSIR_VLM_MODEL or VSIR_EMBED_MODEL, because a floating alias silently changes what the cache keys and the collection fingerprint describe.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/config.py#L78-L83",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:266e3061e85f778abe24320ae44dbc5bf4c5a5fb24541980ce43bbb21623f359:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/doctor.py#L135-L159",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:80c19e14d13c1c37e4a3c2521a6fa18781cf2882426ea0572f76c353aef493c0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_779540fed45943c78de41f8798c336e8",
      "statement": "VSIR_VLM_KEY is optional to load_config but is appended to the required list by the boot check exactly when VSIR_VLM is gemini, so replay mode runs with no credential while a live release cannot start without one.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/tests/unit/test_doctor.py#L196-L205",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4e91a8b4c0222e0057bd230d980638fc53709491091181a8d3c9b3126423879d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/doctor.py#L116-L133",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f155543dce41644202e61ccae9512c7664f71367b00226aeac91b448e2ef52da:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a3af53d5a4234a29921266aebefc496b",
      "statement": "A boot check has three statuses and they carry two different policies: boot refuses on FAIL only, while readiness is red on FAIL or UNAVAILABLE, so an unreachable Qdrant or an absent collection cannot turn a backing-service outage into a restart loop.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/doctor.py#L100-L113",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0ce36ae0d27f8769748e0ac8a2a00fba5cec945c445b82ee1cff18fc1a0ae1ad:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/doctor.py#L22-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1abd10f98569592617154ab2fc437bf2fea165607bd4125c0a9b1c226fc63c36:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/doctor.py#L60-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:85197838f832e0ba46d01707f6cb53913439729be6ac46a53ec6dc127926d60e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_54471aaf342e47d18dff8e04fc6be381",
      "statement": "check_collection_schema asserts the live payload schema against the single INDEXED dict and fails the boot only when the collection exists and disagrees; a collection that does not exist yet is UNAVAILABLE with reason index_not_ready and names `vsir doctor --create-collection` as the remedy.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/doctor.py#L203-L253",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b85f9c4f69108e99dc8731f3e287fbf5e963261f8b4c6654d1ccd7e97c2b8f24:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dc1306e7f17245fdbd04db9cda03305c",
      "statement": "check_collection_fingerprint compares the configured recipe against a record in the control plane rather than the collection, because embed_model and composition_version are not observable from a Qdrant collection; a mismatch refuses the boot since a serving process would otherwise embed queries with one model and compare them against vectors made by another.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/doctor.py#L255-L334",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:27c7af2a56cc2ad93f6b11d63f5ceb3acffdf80a34f690493b16b3cade4da9ab:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6d80ae9e68ca4790aa057dc62845a016",
      "statement": "A pages collection that has never been ingested into has no fingerprint record and passes the fingerprint check, while a stored record that exists but cannot answer the comparison is treated as drift and fails.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/tests/unit/test_doctor.py#L505-L525",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bc8aef4278b74d93183fce0b26cbc05dc0fb3f8b71129ff34b90e8fd6798adeb:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/doctor.py#L306-L334",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:101a671de189f3c2d2b18b9ef3a8389e1226e0388db67e0bb0d42e9d631c8da6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fb23d0d10ba84fa794cab315c228655f",
      "statement": "GET /ready re-runs the full boot check list on every probe in a worker thread rather than reusing the start-up result, so a schema or fingerprint that drifts under a running process turns that instance red instead of leaving it answering.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/serve/app.py#L1386-L1396",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:48ca47a6f6cfaed0cb18b40a595d45b127cdb307f9f59e4e839d99983b7aec47:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_26786c5bc44049acadb211274ca50c5d",
      "statement": "`vsir doctor --create-collection` builds the pages collection from INDEXED and then runs the assertion in one command, as an admin process of the same image rather than a branch inside the server.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/doctor.py#L365-L403",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9425b700a1e1b1846c908b1ccbd7a2065cdcb63dc8b4ba2a235b910ff888f949:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/doctor.py#L480-L495",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8d2662df77edb84db3604f51420c77fbf1de359b30cc8fb9d6b5f5a1c3f303bb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cfac9ea915bc436a93329dda23d14e4f",
      "statement": "The doctor exit event distinguishes a checked pass from an unchecked one: doctor_ok is emitted only when every check concluded, doctor_inconclusive when any check was UNAVAILABLE, and doctor_refused with failed_checks on a refusal.",
      "evidence": [
        {
